    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d458">

                <pb facs="0776" n="656" xml:id="pg656"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">462.00R296A1/63: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Italy
                        (Garrett)</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1932-01-23T15:00:00-05:00">January 23, 1932—3
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>8. Your 13, January 20, noon. The Department’s views in this matter are covered
                    by the <hi rendition="#italic">aide-mémoire</hi> of December 29, sent to you
                    from Paris as Department’s No. 1 and the Department’s 28, January 18, 4 p.m., to
                    Paris, which Paris has sent to you. The texts of these are of course strictly
                    confidential and were given to you for your information and for background in
                    your discussions with Grandi or other competent Italian officials.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Castle</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
